error[E0960]: `G.edge x y` is not a type: it applies a relation to arguments
  --> tests/neg/e0960_unowned_relation.hgn:11:28
   |
11 | edgeIn : {x y : G.node} -> G.edge x y -> tc G ⊢ G.edge x y. (*~ E0960 *)
   |                            ^^^^^^^^^^ an applied relation
   |
   = note: as a meta type, an applied relation would be `⇑(r t̄)`, the lift of a fact type of an application, which no object term has: the fact type of a relation `r` is `r` alone
   = note: an applied relation is a proposition of the program that owns it: a relation of an instance, a module or a functor application `(f ā).r`, or one opened from an instance; a variable's relation is read by every program over it, and a relation of the file or of the enclosing body is not owned yet
   = help: name the program with the turnstile: `P ⊢ G.edge x y`

